# Docker build context filter.
#
# The build context is the REPO ROOT for both entry points — `make build-image`
# runs `docker build ... .` and docker-compose declares `context: ..` — so
# everything below is otherwise shipped to the daemon on every build, and the
# `COPY .diarykg/` line bakes whatever it finds straight into the image.
#
# Mirrors gutenberg_kg/.dockerignore; the entries differ only where this repo
# COPYs `.diarykg/` directly instead of a pre-packed bundle.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Index artefacts that must NOT be baked into the image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DiaryKG's copy of the source corpus (.diarykg/corpus/*.md). `diarykg build`
# writes it so `make reindex` can re-run without the raw text, and `make reindex`
# requires it on disk — but the served handler only ever opens graph.sqlite and
# vectors.sqlite, so in the image it is pure dead weight.
.diarykg/corpus

# Build-only embedding caches — never ship these, they can be several GB.
**/embeddings.json
**/embeddings.jsonl

# Transient SQLite sidecars. The served DB opens fresh, and a WAL copied
# without its DB is worse than useless.
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-journal

# LanceDB stores — dead weight since the sqlite-vec migration (doc-kg >=0.18.2).
# `diarykg build` writes vectors.sqlite and the handler opens only that, but it
# does not delete a lancedb/ dir left over from a pre-migration build, so
# `COPY .diarykg/` would otherwise bake a stale multi-GB index into the image.
**/lancedb

# Snapshots (`diarykg build --snapshot`) — provenance history, not runtime data.
.diarykg/snapshots

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo content the image never reads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source corpus + generated intermediates. The image is served from the built
# index; the 13 MB of raw/enriched text behind it is a build-time input only.
data/

assets/
docs/
analysis/
reports/
config/
scripts/
tests/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.venv/
.venv-image/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Local secrets / env — must never reach a layer
docker/.env
.env
